⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the live-tools rewrite is clobbered when `transformContext` is installed — the fix silently reverts to the run-start snapshot**

The added comment claims "First rewrite, so every later payload rewrite captures the fresh list", but the very next rewrite violates exactly that: when `config.transformContext != null`, `agent_loop.dart:1730-1735` rebuilds `requestContext` with `tools: context.tools` — the *original* run-start snapshot parameter — discarding the `liveTools` rewrite made ten lines above:

```dart
final transformContext = config.transformContext;
if (transformContext != null) {
  requestContext = Context(
    systemPrompt: context.systemPrompt,
    messages: await transformContext(List.of(context.messages), cancelToken),
    tools: context.tools,   // ← run-start snapshot; liveTools is lost
  );
}
```

Every later rewrite in the function correctly threads `requestContext.tools`; only this one reads `context.tools` (harmless before this PR, when the two could never diverge — now they do).

`Agent.transformContext` is public mutable host API (`agent.dart:475`, wired into the config at `agent.dart:950`), so any host that installs the hook reproduces gh-2458 verbatim: the `others` mount re-syncs `state.tools`, `toolsProvider` resolves the fresh list, and the transformContext rebuild throws it away — the mounted tool stays invisible to the provider for the rest of the run. No in-repo host sets the hook today, which is why this is ⚠️ and not 🚨; the moment one does, this is the original bug with a green test suite (the new tests never install a `transformContext`).

One-line fix: use `tools: requestContext.tools` in the transformContext rebuild (it is non-null there whenever `toolsProvider` returned a list, falling back to the snapshot otherwise), plus a test case in `gh2458_midloop_mount_test.dart` that installs a `transformContext` hook alongside `toolsProvider`.
